Package: kmod-trelay
Version: 6.6.133-r2
Depends: kernel (=6.6.133~4ce96c40f56e48b979f188be26ebbd8b-r1)
Source: feeds/base/kernel/trelay
SourceName: trelay
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1594830836
Architecture: aarch64_cortex-a53
Installed-Size: 30720
Filename: kmod-trelay_6.6.133-r2_aarch64_cortex-a53.ipk
Size: 4943
SHA256sum: 4d3f8b7da3ce91c63703822b0014b10ca945e6f6214a8254f043b2ead1a03835
Description:  trelay relays ethernet packets between two devices (similar to a bridge), but
 without any MAC address checks. This makes it possible to bridge client mode
 or ad-hoc mode wifi devices to ethernet VLANs, assuming the remote end uses
 the same source MAC address as the device that packets are supposed to exit
 from.

